# Architecture boundaries

- Authoritative rules belong in `packages/sim-core` or `packages/battle-sim`.
- `apps/client` converts input to commands and state/events to presentation.
- Phaser scenes must not calculate canonical combat, economy, AI, research, movement, or random outcomes.
- React must not own per-frame entity state or render one component per battlefield soldier.
- Simulation packages must not import Phaser, React, DOM, browser storage, network clients, timers, or wall-clock APIs.
- Storage adapters serialize/validate simulation snapshots; simulation does not know IndexedDB.
- Content files are loaded and validated at the boundary; hot simulation code consumes resolved definitions.
- Cross-package contracts use discriminated unions and version fields.
- Add an ADR when dependency direction, save compatibility, or the simulation/render split changes.
